WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
A snooker player strikes the white ball.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:06.920
It rolls fast up the table,
towards a red ball sitting still.

3
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:07.850
Click.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.470
The white ball slows, and
the red one shoots away.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.010
The total momentum of the two
balls is the same before and after.

6
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.140
That holds in every collision.

7
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.590
But what about their energy of motion?

8
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.130
Momentum is conserved,
but is kinetic energy?

9
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:29.230
In this mission, you'll find a neat way to
get kinetic energy straight from momentum.

10
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.270
Then you'll follow two pucks
that glance off each other,

11
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.330
and track momentum in
two directions at once.

12
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: decide whether two colliding
snooker balls keep their kinetic energy.
